<header><p class="st-kicker">kingdom · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Kingdom of the Gepids</h1><p class="st-meta">454 CE – 567 CE · capital Sirmium</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">East Germanic kingdom in the Tisza plain and Transylvania that rose after Attila's empire collapsed and was destroyed by Lombards and Avars in 567.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gepids">Gepids</a>, a Gothic-related people, were subjects of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attila">Attila's</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/huns">Huns</a>. In 454 their king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ardaric">Ardaric</a> led the revolt that crushed Attila's sons at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-nedao">River Nedao</a>, and the Gepids took over the lands east of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a> plain and <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-transylvania">Transylvania</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>Gepid kings ruled a mixed population of Germanic, Sarmatian and local peoples, and adopted Arian <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christianity">Christianity</a>. Rich princely graves such as those at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/apahida">Apahida</a> show their wealth. They seized <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sirmium">Sirmium</a> (Sremska Mitrovica) on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sava">Sava</a>, a key city, and competed with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ostrogoths">Ostrogoths</a>, <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/byzantium">Byzantium</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a> for the middle <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a>. Kings <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thurisind">Thurisind</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunimund">Cunimund</a> fought the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-the-lombards">Lombards</a> in the 550s and 560s.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>In 567 the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lombards">Lombards</a> under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alboin">Alboin</a>, allied with the newly arrived <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avars">Avars</a>, destroyed the kingdom; <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cunimund">Cunimund</a> was killed and Alboin made his skull into a drinking cup. The Gepid lands passed to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/avar-khaganate">Avar Khaganate</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/kingdom-of-the-gepids.jpg" alt="Kingdom of the Gepids" width="320" height="222"><figcaption>Image: Guriezous · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Europe_and_the_Near_East_at_476_AD.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>454 CE – 567 CE</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/5th-century">5th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/6th-century">6th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>kingdom</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Sirmium</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Ardaric, Thurisind, Cunimund</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Arian Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Gepid (East Germanic)</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a>, <a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/serbia">Serbia</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Gepid Kingdom, Gepidia</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=510&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-gepids" aria-label="Kingdom of the Gepids on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5147 590 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Kingdom of the Gepids lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5467 846h0"/><path class="map-dot-me" d="M5467 846h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>The dot marks Sirmium. <a href="/atlas?year=510&amp;focus=kingdom-of-the-gepids">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>
